GroovyMAME nogpu pacing: recreate the socket to RAISE the pacing rate (2026-11-01)

Incremental fix for a fork that already has groovymame-mister-pacing.patch as first
published (2026-10-30); a fresh checkout applies the updated groovymame-mister-pacing.patch.

Raising the rate (2026-11-01 fix): Linux can only LOWER a UDP socket's pacing rate
(SO_MAX_PACING_RATE sets sk_pacing_rate = min(sk_pacing_rate, rate); TCP recomputes it,
UDP never raises it). After a narrower mode (256 px wide, 8.25 MB/s) the next wider one
(320 px, 10.3 MB/s) stayed at 8.25 MB/s: frames queued up, the FPGA's ACKs came ~24
lines later every frame until GroovyMAME lost sync (timeouts, sound and picture broken).
To go up, the socket is recreated on the same local port.

